      ":question/id": "0dfb24ed-71db-576c-87d7-7b45fd0ad875",
      ":question/problem": "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}{r}^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ {r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g\u22a5h$ and $r>0$, find the value of $r.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $g\u22a5h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot {r}^{2}+(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}-2{r}^{2}-6 \\\\  & =2{r}^{2}-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =3 \\\\ r & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $r>0.$ Therefore, $r=\\sqrt{3}.$"
    },
