      ":question/id": "38cba23b-122c-5771-b6e6-8755391889ee",
      ":question/problem": "Let $u=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $u\u22a5v$ and $a<0$, find the value of $a.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $u\u22a5v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y}+{u}_{z}\\cdot {v}_{z} \\\\  & =a\\cdot a+2\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={a}^{2}-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =10 \\\\ a & =\\pm \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $a<0.$ Therefore, $a=-\\sqrt{10}.$"
    },
