      ":question/id": "d00137d5-07f7-5c87-9146-2b0f0101752e",
      ":question/problem": "Let $a=\u27e8{x}^{2},-1\u27e9$ and $b=\u27e82,2\u27e9.$ If $a\u22a5b$ and $x<0,$ then $x=${{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $a\u22a5b$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $a\\cdot b=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $x<0.$ Therefore, $x=-1.$"
